  "appliesTo": "We are responsible for setting holiday and term dates for community and voluntary controlled schools.",
  "academyNote": "The term dates for foundation and voluntary aided schools are decided by their governing bodies. Term dates vary for each school; please check with the school for their holiday dates.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Bolton's 2026/27 pattern equates to 197 days, so governing boards have the authority to set 7 occasional days to meet local needs.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/6212/school-term-dates-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Bolton asks schools to place their 5 INSET days outside the published term time.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/6212/school-term-dates-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2026/27 summer term runs to Friday 23 July 2027 and the next school year starts on Monday 6 September 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/6212/school-term-dates-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "In 2027/28 the pattern equates to 192 days, with 2 occasional days for governing boards to set.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/7254/school-term-dates-2027-2028"
    },
    {
      "fact": "If a school is used as a polling station for the local elections on Thursday 6 May 2027 and has to close, one of its occasional days should be used for the closure.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/6212/school-term-dates-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Bolton's February half term in 2028 is Monday 21 to Friday 25 February.",
      "source": "https://www.bolton.gov.uk/downloads/file/7254/school-term-dates-2027-2028"
    }
  ],
